\f0\b\fs69\fsmilli34667 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Installing Minion 2\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa560\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs32 \cf3 \strokec3 Your private memory, upgraded. Takes about two minutes of your time.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa333\partightenfactor0

\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf2 \strokec2 Minion 2 brings everything from your current Minion over automatically \'97 you won't lose a single note. Just follow these steps in order.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf2 1. Put Minion 2 in your Applications\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa140\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 You've already opened this folder, so you can see 
\f2\b Minion 2
\f1\b0  sitting next to this guide.\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Drag 
\f2\b Minion 2
\f1\b0  into your 
\f2\b Applications
\f1\b0  folder.\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Double-click it to open.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa306\partightenfactor0

\fs30\fsmilli15333 \cf3 \strokec3 If macOS says 
\f3\i "Minion 2 can't be opened because Apple cannot check it"
\f1\i0 : right-click the app, choose 
\f2\b Open
\f1\b0 , then click 
\f2\b Open
\f1\b0  again. You only do this once.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf2 \strokec2 2. Let it bring your memory over\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa333\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf2 The first time it opens, Minion 2 copies everything from your old Minion by itself. There is nothing for you to click.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa140\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Your notes are searchable within 
\f2\b seconds
\f1\b0 .\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The smarter, deeper search keeps sharpening quietly in the background for up to an hour. You can use the app the whole time.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Your old Minion is left completely untouched, just in case.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf2 3. Check that Claude can see your notes\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa333\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf2 Minion 2 reconnects Claude to your memory automatically. Open Claude and ask it something only your notes would know. When it answers, you're all set.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa306\partightenfactor0

\fs30\fsmilli15333 \cf3 \strokec3 If Claude comes up empty, fully quit Claude (
\f4 \cb4 Cmd\'a0+\'a0Q
\f1 \cb1 ) and reopen it.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32 \cf2 \cb4 \strokec2 Important last step.
\f1\b0  Once Claude is working with Minion 2, please remove the 
\f3\i old
\f1\i0  Minion \'97 otherwise the two versions quietly fight over Claude. It only takes a moment (next page... er, next section).\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf2 \cb1 4. Remove the old Minion\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa140\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0
\f1\b0\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 In the menu bar at the top of your screen, find the old 
\f2\b Minion
\f1\b0  icon, click it, and choose 
\f2\b Quit
\f1\b0 .\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Open 
\f2\b System Settings \uc0\u8594  General \u8594  Login Items
\f1\b0 , select 
\f2\b Minion
\f1\b0  in the list, and click the minus (
\f2\b \'96
\f1\b0 ) button so it stops starting up on its own.\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Open your 
\f2\b Applications
\f1\b0  folder, find the old 
\f2\b Minion
\f1\b0  (the one 
\f3\i without
\f1\i0  the "2"), and drag it to the Trash.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa333\partightenfactor0
\cf2 That's it. Minion 2 is now your memory, and Claude is pointed at it.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf5 \strokec5 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf2 \strokec2 If something looks off\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa140\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0
\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Search feels thin at first
\f1\b0  \'97 that's normal in the first hour while the deeper search finishes building. Keyword search works right away.\
\ls4\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Claude isn't finding anything
\f1\b0  \'97 quit Claude fully (
\f4\fs30\fsmilli15333 \cb4 Cmd\'a0+\'a0Q
\f1\fs33\fsmilli16667 \cb1 ) and reopen it.\
\ls4\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 You're ever unsure
\f1\b0  \'97 your old Minion still has all your original data and still works. Nothing was deleted. You can always fall back to it.\
